 "notes": "ICMP 'port 10000' is unusual (AWS ICMP rules normally use -1), but the prompt states it and the GT plans it, so the port is kept as a detail check (sg_icmp_egress_port) while the core ICMP check tests the protocol only; real templates writing -1 fail that detail check because they contradict the prompt. Protocols accept the name or IANA number (tcp/6, udp/17, icmp/1). The all-protocols rule checks protocol -1/all with port 0 (inline and aws_security_group_rule); aws_vpc_security_group_egress_rule with ip_protocol -1 carries no ports."
